+ * accepted (four-digit year, two-digit month and day, ASCII digits, nothing before or after), and it must be a
+ * real calendar date: "2026-02-30", "2026-13-01", "2026-00-10", "2026-04-31" and "2023-02-29" are errors, while
+ * "2024-02-29", "2000-02-29" are fine and "1900-02-29" is not. Years outside 0000 to 9999 use the extended form
+ * that formatIsoDate writes, a sign and six digits ("+012024-01-05", "-000001-12-31"); "-000000" is not allowed,
+ * as in ISO 8601. A time of day ("2024-01-05T10:00Z"), spaces, other separators and shorter forms are errors,
+ * and so are dates beyond what a Date can hold. The text is not trimmed.
